WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.467 --> 00:00:18.472
"How many of you make your own lunches?" Miss Shelly asked.

2
00:00:18.473 --> 00:00:22.904
Ethan, Bobby, Jason, Izzie, and Nina sat on the rug.

3
00:00:22.905 --> 00:00:26.221
It was another day of Kids Central.

4
00:00:26.222 --> 00:00:28.198
Nina spoke up.

5
00:00:28.199 --> 00:00:32.006
"I don't, but my mom wishes I did."

6
00:00:32.007 --> 00:00:37.086
"Well, today you will make a sandwich by yourself," Miss Shelly said.

7
00:00:37.087 --> 00:00:40.110
"You can bring it to school tomorrow for lunch."

8
00:00:40.111 --> 00:00:46.969
Jason smiled. That would make his busy parents happy!

9
00:00:46.970 --> 00:00:52.682
"We have ingredients here to make tuna or egg salad sandwiches.

10
00:00:52.683 --> 00:00:56.630
Decide which one you want to make," Miss Shelly said.

11
00:00:56.631 --> 00:00:59.975
Nina and Ethan chose tuna salad.

12
00:00:59.976 --> 00:01:03.904
Jason, Bobby, and Izzie chose egg salad.

13
00:01:03.905 --> 00:01:07.867
"Egg salad makers, you have to boil your eggs.

14
00:01:07.868 --> 00:01:10.850
So place your eggs in a pot of water.

15
00:01:10.851 --> 00:01:16.773
I'll turn on the burner," Miss Shelly said.

16
00:01:16.774 --> 00:01:20.442
"Let's mix the mayonnaise now," Izzie said.

17
00:01:20.443 --> 00:01:22.261
"While we wait."

18
00:01:22.262 --> 00:01:29.615
"Good idea." Bobby nodded and reached for the mayonnaise.

19
00:01:29.616 --> 00:01:39.020
"Mix mayonnaise with mustard," Jason read.

20
00:01:39.021 --> 00:01:46.546
"And here are the chopped cucumbers," Izzie said.

21
00:01:46.547 --> 00:01:50.326
"Tuna salad makers," Miss Shelly said.

22
00:01:50.327 --> 00:01:53.377
"You need to open your cans."

23
00:01:53.378 --> 00:01:57.096
Ethan picked up a can opener and placed it on the can.

24
00:01:57.097 --> 00:02:04.107
Twist, twist, twist. He opened his can.

25
00:02:04.108 --> 00:02:07.414
"How'd you do that?" Nina asked.

26
00:02:07.415 --> 00:02:11.220
"I turned the handle, but nothing happened!"

27
00:02:11.221 --> 00:02:15.009
"Maybe the blade didn't cut through the metal," Ethan said.

28
00:02:15.010 --> 00:02:17.435
"Squeeze the handles shut, like this."

29
00:02:17.436 --> 00:02:19.873
Ethan showed her how.

30
00:02:19.874 --> 00:02:24.856
"Thanks." Nina smiled.

31
00:02:24.857 --> 00:02:41.537
"Now we drain the tuna and mix the mayonnaise with salt and cucumber."

32
00:02:41.538 --> 00:02:43.673
"The eggs are ready!

33
00:02:43.674 --> 00:02:48.205
Time to peel and chop," Bobby said.

34
00:02:48.206 --> 00:02:53.620
Miss Shelly nodded. "You peel, I'll cut."

35
00:02:53.621 --> 00:02:55.354
"No, we'll chop them,"

36
00:02:55.355 --> 00:02:58.244
Jason said, reaching for the knife.

37
00:02:58.245 --> 00:03:01.798
"We're supposed to make lunch by ourselves."

38
00:03:01.799 --> 00:03:05.497
"Be careful, Jason," Miss Shelly warned.

39
00:03:05.498 --> 00:03:08.681
She watched him chop an egg.

40
00:03:08.682 --> 00:03:13.613
"You know, getting help is still okay sometimes," she added.

41
00:03:13.614 --> 00:03:17.922
The egg salad makers mixed their eggs with their mayonnaise.

42
00:03:17.923 --> 00:03:22.100
The tuna salad makers mixed their tuna with their mayonnaise.

43
00:03:22.101 --> 00:03:27.909
"We're ready to make sandwiches!" the two groups cried at the same time.

44
00:03:27.910 --> 00:03:32.069
Miss Shelly laughed. "Good work, chefs!"

45
00:03:32.070 --> 00:03:35.640
The kids spread their salads onto pieces of bread.

46
00:03:35.641 --> 00:03:39.829
Then they put another piece of bread on top.

47
00:03:39.830 --> 00:03:42.619
"Now we'll wrap your sandwiches.

48
00:03:42.620 --> 00:03:45.527
You can bring them for lunch tomorrow!"

49
00:03:45.528 --> 00:03:48.731
Miss Shelly handed out sheets of paper.

50
00:03:48.732 --> 00:03:51.146
"This is special paper.

51
00:03:51.147 --> 00:03:54.266
It will keep your sandwiches fresh."

52
00:03:54.267 --> 00:03:57.316
They folded the paper around the sandwiches.

53
00:03:57.317 --> 00:03:59.963
But Jason was having trouble.

54
00:03:59.964 --> 00:04:03.597
"Mine doesn't work!" he said.

55
00:04:03.598 --> 00:04:09.458
"Can I help you, Jason?" Miss Shelly asked. Jason nodded.

56
00:04:09.459 --> 00:04:16.720
"Try putting your sandwich in the center of the paper," she said.

57
00:04:16.721 --> 00:04:20.924
When it was time to go home, Jason ran to his mom.

58
00:04:20.925 --> 00:04:25.168
"I made my lunch for tomorrow. All by myself!"

59
00:04:25.169 --> 00:04:28.045
He looked at his teacher.

60
00:04:28.046 --> 00:04:31.096
"But Miss Shelly helped," he added.

61
00:04:31.097 --> 00:04:39.511
"Sometimes a little help is okay."
